    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "idk, it just feels like \"finding a balance\" is often used as an excuse to keep everything complicated. if the goal is growth, shouldn't the default be to strip away as much as possible unless there's a super obvious reason not to? like, isn't the \"precautionary principle\" just a way to stall progress?",
